      "content": "<h3>3. computeIfAbsent, merge and the other compute methods</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Signature:</strong> <code>compute / computeIfAbsent / computeIfPresent / merge</code></li>\n<li><strong>Returns:</strong> as HashMap</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> O(1)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>For freshers:</strong> They behave exactly as in HashMap. A new key created by one of them is added at the end of the order.</p>\n<p><strong>For experienced developers:</strong> When you build a grouped or counted result that you later print, LinkedHashMap gives you the groups in the order they were first seen.</p>",
